# sha256 of the release assets bootstrap.sh installs into agent/bin: fd, rg,
# jq, yq, shellcheck, ast-grep, uv, mlr, resvg and pixi. Not every project publishes
# checksums in a form this can read at install time, so the pinned versions are
# recorded here and checked exactly the way the Node tarball is.
#
# Keyed `tool/version/asset`, not by asset name alone: jq and yq publish their
# binaries under names with no version in them (jq-macos-amd64, yq_darwin_amd64),
# so an asset-only key would hand a pinned 1.8.2 checksum to a 1.7.1 download
# and abort on a mismatch that is really a stale lookup.
#
# To pin a new version: change the *_VERSION default in bootstrap.sh, download
# that tool's four assets and add their `shasum -a 256` output below under the
# new key. A version that is not listed here still installs - verified against
# the project's own published checksum where there is one, unverified and with
# a warning where there is not.
#
# fd 10.4 and later are built against a macOS SDK newer than the Intel Macs in
# the estate, so x86_64-apple-darwin stays on 10.3.0 - the same pin pi uses.
# ast-grep publishes no musl build, so its Linux assets are the glibc ones.
